 "notes": "Curve digitised from Figure 19 of the paper (combined 95% CL exclusion on kinetic mixing chi from resonant and broadband WISPDMX signal scans, Eq. 5.2, rho_DM = 0.3 GeV/cm^3, V = 447 L, isotropic hidden-photon polarization assumption). The WISPDMX curve in figure19.pdf of the e-print is stored as two embedded raster layers (filled excluded region + limit line); the lower boundary of the excluded region was extracted per pixel column with axes calibrated from the vector gridlines (x: log10 m from -10 to 0, y: log10 chi from -16 to -4), then downsampled to a 0.045-dex grid (median within each bin) with the three deep resonant-mode dips (TM010 ~0.86 ueV, TE111 ~1.34 ueV, TM020 ~1.89 ueV, chi ~3-4e-14) added explicitly. Curve spans 1e-10 eV to 2.07e-6 eV as plotted; the paper quotes improvement over previous limits for 0.4 neV to 2.07 ueV. Plateau level ~1e-12 over 0.2-2.07 ueV matches the abstract. Bottom envelope of the plotted noisy limit curve was used (the visible boundary of the shaded excluded region); the instantaneous limit fluctuates upward from it in RFI channels.",
